.Dd June 13, 2026
.Dt QSTAR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qstar
.Nd standalone QStar build graph evaluator and local executor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -file Ar qstar.lua
.Op Fl G Ar stella|ninja|auto
.Op Fl B Ar path
.Op Fl -color Ar auto|always|never
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Ar docs
.Op Fl -path | Fl -ai-index | Fl -show Ar wiki-relative.md
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
evaluates QStar authoring files, validates a target graph, renders command
plans, and runs a limited local executor for build, test, install, stage, and
external smoke actions.
The project entrypoint is
.Pa qstar.lua .
Subdirectory fragments use the
.Pa .qst
suffix.
Helper modules use the
.Pa .qsm
suffix and are imported through
.Ic qstar.import_module .
.Pp
QStar is a generic build system.
C, C++, assembler, and Cale are supported through language namespaces and
toolchain profiles, but QStar does not interpret Cale or HCL semantics itself.
Generated actions use
.Ic qstar.cli
argv vectors, not shell strings.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--generator"
.It Fl -file Ar qstar.lua
Select the root QStar entrypoint.
.It Fl G Ar stella|ninja|auto
Select the effective generator.
In this release,
.Ar auto
resolves to
.Ar stella .
.Ar stella
runs the local Stella executor.
.Ar ninja
emits and runs a Ninja backend for C/C++/ASM compile, generated actions,
static libraries, executable/test links, run target wrappers, and group phony
targets.
Stage and install copy/manifest work is still performed by QStar, but referenced
target artifacts are built through the effective generator.
.It Fl -generator Ar stella|ninja|auto
Alias for
.Fl G .
.It Fl B Ar path
Override
.Ic qstar.project
build_dir with a package-relative build directory.
.It Fl -color Ar auto|always|never
Control ANSI color for text output.
JSON diagnostics are never colorized.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "list-targets"
.It Ic version
Print the QStar version. The
.Fl -version
form is equivalent.
.It Ic docs
Print local documentation entrypoints, including the wiki and AI index.
Use
.Fl -show
to print a specific wiki document such as
.Pa reference/modules.md .
.It Ic list-targets
List graph targets. Use
.Fl -format Ar json
for the stable machine-readable target listing, including effective generator,
build_dir, generated_dir, compile_commands policy, configs, and installability.
.It Ic query
Print one target, generated action, stage, or config by label.
.It Ic doctor
Inspect profile and toolchain resolution, external tools, sysroot/resource_dir,
response file policy, depfile behavior, and writable build state.
.It Ic check
Evaluate the graph and validate packages, labels, generated outputs, sources,
headers, profiles, and file inputs without running build actions.
.It Ic lint
Evaluate authoring diagnostics without executing build actions.
.It Ic fmt
Format
.Pa qstar.lua ,
.Pa .qst ,
or
.Pa .qsm
files. Use
.Fl -check
for verification and
.Fl -stdout
to print the formatted text.
.It Ic explain
Print target closure and command-plan information.
.It Ic dry-run
Render action plans without running them.
.It Ic emit-ninja
Emit
.Pa build/qstar/ninja/build.ninja
and the policy-controlled
.Pa compile_commands.json
without running Ninja.
The Ninja backend lowers C/C++/ASM compile actions,
.Ic qstar.configure_file ,
.Ic qstar.custom_target ,
static libraries, shared libraries on Darwin-like and Linux-like profiles,
executable/test links, and
.Ic qstar.run_target
wrappers, plus
.Ic qstar.group
phony targets.
Stage/install copy and manifest actions remain QStar-owned.
Cale source actions are Stella-only language-provider actions in this release and still require the
.Ar stella
generator.
QStar does not interpret Cale or HCL semantics itself.
Windows DLL/import-library/PDB shared library policy is deferred.
.It Ic build
Build using the effective generator.
The
.Ar stella
generator runs the local Stella executor.
The
.Ar ninja
generator emits
.Pa build/qstar/ninja/build.ninja
and invokes
.Xr ninja 1
for the supported MVP graph.
Build accepts
.Fl -jobs Ar N ,
.Fl -schedule-trace ,
.Fl -verbose ,
.Fl -quiet ,
and
.Fl -progress Ar auto|plain|off .
Default output is compact progress plus the final build summary.
Verbose output adds status lines and
.Li build_action
events, and schedule trace enables deterministic scheduler events.
.Pp
The QStar 0.5 progress contract uses CMake-style action descriptions:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[  8%] Building C object build/qstar/out/__core/obj0.o
[ 75%] Linking CXX executable app
[100%] Built target app
.Ed
.Pp
General output must not expose legacy scheduler stage wording,
.Li Status: compiling ,
.Li schedule_action ,
or
.Li build_action
records.
Those details belong to
.Fl -verbose
or
.Fl -schedule-trace .
Stella observes child stdout/stderr line by line and highlights the
.Li warning:
prefix in orange/yellow. It highlights the
.Li error:
prefix in bold red.
.Fl -color Ar never
and non-TTY output disable ANSI color, and JSON diagnostics remain uncolored.
.Pp
Action descriptions are also preserved in action-log and replay metadata.
.Ic qstar action-log ,
.Ic qstar replay ,
and
.Ic qstar last-failure
print the same
.Li description=
metadata used by progress output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
description='Building C object build/qstar/out/___app/obj0.o'
.Ed
For the Stella executor, successful and cache-hit action
.Pa .log
files are not a public contract. They may be lazily reconstructed from
compact state and the current graph when
.Ic action-log
or
.Ic replay
is requested. Failed actions and the last-failure replay are still written
immediately.
.It Ic test
Build and run QStar test targets.
.It Ic install
Build a target artifact if needed, copy it into a prefix, and write install
manifest state. Use
.Fl -dry-run
to preview the copy plan.
.It Ic stage
Create a copy-only staged package tree.
.It Ic why-rebuild
Explain cache state and why a target would rebuild.
.It Ic clean
Remove the effective build directory, or a single target output with
.Fl -target Ar label .
.It Ic log
Print the latest logical action log paths for a target.
.It Ic last-failure
Print the latest failure replay file and action description metadata.
.It Ic action-log
Print argv/env/input/output log and description metadata for an action id.
.It Ic replay
Print the replay command and description metadata for an action id.
.It Ic lsp
Run the QStar language server with
.Fl -stdio .
.It Ic init
Create a starter project from
.Ar c-app ,
.Ar c-lib ,
.Ar generated ,
or
.Ar mixed-cale .
.It Ic --dump-graph
Print the raw Graph IR for debugging and drift tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md"
.It Pa qstar.lua
Project root entrypoint.
.It Pa *.qst
QStar fragment file.
.It Pa *.qsm
QStar helper module file.
.It Pa build/qstar
Default state, log, response file, build artifact, stage, and compile database
directory.
.It Pa generated
Default
.Ic qstar.project
generated_dir for generated action outputs.
.It Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/README.md
Installed QStar wiki entrypoint.
.It Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md
Short documentation map for AI agents and automation.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "QSTAR_DOC_DIR"
.It Ev QSTAR_DOC_DIR
Overrides the documentation directory printed by
.Nm
.Ic docs .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qstar-lua 5 ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/README.md ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md
